\section{Re-exporting the public surface}

The package root exists to make the common use cases discoverable.
Users should not need to remember where the CLI helpers or the model
objects live internally.

<<imports>>=
from pytorial.cli import add_argparse_subcommand
from pytorial.cli import add_typer_subcommand
from pytorial.cli import create_app
from pytorial.catalog import TutorialCatalog
from pytorial.catalog import get_tutorial
from pytorial.catalog import get_tutorials
from pytorial.model import StepTranscript
from pytorial.model import TextMatch
from pytorial.model import Tutorial
from pytorial.model import TutorialRun
from pytorial.model import TutorialStep
from pytorial.run import RunResult
from pytorial.run import TutorialRunner
from pytorial.shell import posix_terminal_available
from pytorial.shell import run_interactive_shell
from pytorial.shell import run_scripted_shell
from pytorial.state import ProgressState
from pytorial.state import StateStore
@

One export is missing from that list on purpose.  [[app]], the ready-made
standalone application, can only be built once Typer is imported, and
the CLI chapter goes to some length to keep Typer out of hosts that are
built on [[argparse]] (\cref{tutorial-cli-deferred-typer}).  Importing
[[app]] eagerly here would undo that for every host.  The package
therefore hands it out the same way [[pytorial.cli]] does, through a
module [[__getattr__]]: [[pytorial.app]] and [[from pytorial import app]]
keep working, and the cost moves to whoever actually asks for it.

<<lazy exports>>=
def __getattr__(name: str):
    """Build the standalone application when ``app`` is first requested."""

    if name == "app":
        from pytorial import cli

        return cli.app
    raise AttributeError(f"module {__name__!r} has no attribute {name!r}")
@

Let's verify that the package exports the file-backed lookup helpers and
the CLI integration helpers, the lazily built [[app]] among them.

<<test functions>>=
def test_package_exports_catalog_helpers():
    assert callable(get_tutorial)
    assert callable(get_tutorials)
    assert TutorialCatalog.__name__ == "TutorialCatalog"


def test_package_exports_cli_helpers():
    assert callable(create_app)
    assert callable(add_typer_subcommand)
    assert callable(add_argparse_subcommand)


def test_package_builds_the_standalone_app_on_request():
    import typer

    import pytorial
    import pytorial.cli

    assert isinstance(pytorial.app, typer.Typer)
    assert pytorial.app is pytorial.cli.app
@

The embedding helpers register the tutorial group on every platform and
let its help text say where shell steps can run, so a host needs no
platform logic of its own.  We still export the predicate behind that
help text: a host that wants to word its own note, or to skip a
tutorial-related hint elsewhere in its interface, should ask the same
question the runner asks rather than inspect [[sys.platform]].

<<test functions>>=
def test_package_exports_platform_predicate():
    assert posix_terminal_available() is True
